<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Atlantic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1939–1945</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Atlantic was the longest continuous campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, fought between Allied navies and air forces and German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/u-boat">U-boats</a> and surface raiders over the convoy routes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. The Royal Canadian Navy grew into one of the largest Allied navies in the struggle. Allied victory, clear by mid-1943, made the invasion of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> possible.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-atlantic.jpg" alt="Battle of the Atlantic" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Post-Work: User:W.wolny · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Officers_on_the_bridge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
